PLUGIN MARKET RESEARCH: ANTI-REPETITION / LOOP GUARDS
====================================================
Time : 2026-10-13 21:44

WHERE THE MARKET IS
  DSH plugins are npm packages. Sources used: registry.npmmirror.com (mirror) and registry.npmjs.org.
  A community catalogue exists at dsh-plugin.org (pack badges reference it); dsh.so adds risk badges.
  GUI entry: sidebar Plugins page. The settings "Built-in plugins" section is a read-only inventory.
  CLI: dsh plugin --profile <p> add <pkg>; the local dsh CLI is present at %APPDATA%\npm\dsh.ps1.
  The desktop profile is owned by the app, so CLI installs are rejected there - use the in-app page.

WHY THE BUILT-IN GUARDS CANNOT CATCH THIS
  dsh-agent-loop's own Chinese README states there is NO built-in turn budget, and the shipped guards
  hang off tool execution (guard/timeout-policy on tools/execute, guard/repeat-tool-reminder on
  tools/post-execute with a chain key of (tool name, canonical arguments)). A degeneration loop emits
  only reasoning-delta - zero text-delta, zero tool-call-delta - so neither guard fires, turnEnds stays
  null and the turn cannot settle. That is the "it stopped by itself" event, reproduced from the source.

FOUR MATCHING PLUGINS (all MIT, all compatible with this machine's 0.2.0-rc.2)
  dsh-guard-repeat-output   2.1.7  host-side: sanitize code points, detect collapse, DISCARD the attempt
                                   before it enters history, and retroactively clean a poisoned session.
                                   Its README documents production incidents of 1.37M chars ("Let me
                                   produce." x27269) and 250K chars ("Let me write." x1958).
  dsh-dupguard              1.9.1  stops generation when the same string repeats >=10 times; reasoning
                                   text included; code regions relaxed 3x; threshold adjustable in settings.
  @mrweicodes/dsh-loop-guard 1.0.9 takes over llm/stream, breaks reasoning-only and restated-material
                                   degenerations from inside the stream, then injects a correction so the
                                   task continues. Its README describes exactly the "好。执行。" pattern.
  dsh-local-loop-fuse       0.8.3  three lines: text/reasoning repetition (abortable), low-diversity
                                   sliding window, no-progress stall, then agent.cancel().
  (also dsh-task-reliability 0.4.9 - a bundle with n-gram reasoning-repeat intervention plus retries,
   auto-continue, resume-after-sleep, truncation top-up, autopilot; needs Node >=22.)
  The official @deepseek-ai/dsh-repeat-tool-reminder only watches tool calls and only advises - useless
  for a loop that makes no tool calls at all.

COMPATIBILITY VERIFIED ON THIS MACHINE
  dsh-desktop-runtime / dsh-llm / dsh-agent / dsh-agent-loop all 0.2.0-rc.2
  loop-guard requires dsh-llm and dsh-agent in >=0.2.0-alpha.1 <0.3.0  -> satisfies
  schemastery 3.18.4 (^3.18.1 ok), cordis 4.0.4 (^4.0.2 ok), Node 24.20.0 (>=20 / >=22 ok)

RECOMMENDATION
  Install ONE of them (they mostly share the llm/stream mount point, so stacking them risks interference).
  For this incident the strongest fit is dsh-guard-repeat-output (does not let the garbage reach history
  and can clean an already-poisoned session); the simplest is dsh-dupguard; the least disruptive is
  @mrweicodes/dsh-loop-guard because it resumes the task after breaking the loop.
  Install via the in-app Plugins page, then RESTART DSH, then confirm the plugin's own startup line in
  the host log before trusting it.